@* Progress's Overview, written by hand after Badge's: a value and its label, sizes and colors, the
   indeterminate bar, and a bar that C# moves on an interactive page. Accessibility and See also
   come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A progress bar shows how far along a task is. It suits work with a length you can measure, such as an upload or an import. Without a value, it shows that the task is still working. For a wait with nothing to measure in a small space, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/spinner">Spinner</Anchor>. For content that's still loading, put a <Anchor Href="docs/components/skeleton">Skeleton</Anchor> in its place. For the steps of a form, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/stepper">Stepper</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Value and label</Heading>
<TextBlock>The bar fills to its <Code>Value</Code>, out of <Code>Max</Code>, which is 100 by default. Its <Code>Label</Code> is the line above the bar, and also its name for screen readers. To show the percentage at the end of that line, set <Code>ShowValue</Code>. To show your own text there instead, such as "3 of 5 files", set <Code>ValueText</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="progress-values" />
<TextBlock>Screen readers hear the same text: <Code>ValueText</Code>, or the percentage. A value below 0 or above <Code>Max</Code> shows as the nearest end.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Sizes and colors</Heading>
<TextBlock>The size sets the bar's thickness: Sm, Md or Lg, to sit with controls of that size. Set <Code>Size</Code> to choose one. The bar uses the primary color by default. To change it, set <Code>Accent</Code>, such as <Code>Accent.From(Color.Warning)</Code> for a status color, or <Code>Accent.Of("#0d9488")</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="progress-sizes" />
<TextBlock>The color doesn't reach screen readers. When the color means a warning, say so in the label or the value text too, such as "almost full".</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Indeterminate</Heading>
<TextBlock>An indeterminate bar sweeps across while the work has no known length. Leave out <Code>Value</Code>. A bar without a <Code>Label</Code> needs an <Code>aria-label</Code> for its name.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="progress-indeterminate" />
<TextBlock>With reduced motion, the sweep is slower. Once you know how much work there is, set <Code>Value</Code>, and the bar starts to fill.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Circle</Heading>
<TextBlock>Set <Code>Shape</Code> to <Code>ProgressShape.Circle</Code> to show the progress as a circle, for a dashboard or a card. It fills clockwise from the top. <Code>ShowValue</Code> and <Code>ValueText</Code> put the value in the middle, and the <Code>Label</Code> goes under the circle. <Code>Size</Code> sets the diameter: 2rem, 3rem or 5rem. At Sm, the value goes beside the label. For any other diameter, set <Code>Width</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="progress-circle" />
<TextBlock>Without a <Code>Value</Code>, an arc turns around the circle. Every other parameter works as it does on the bar, and screen readers hear the same name and value.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Updating from C#</Heading>
<TextBlock>The bar renders on the server, so on <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">static pages</Anchor> it shows the value from when the page rendered. On interactive pages, change <Code>Value</Code> from C#, and the bar follows.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="progress-from-code" />

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <Progress Value="40" Label="Uploading report.pdf" ShowValue />
        <Progress Value="3" Max="5" Label="Importing" ValueText="3 of 5 files" />

        @* No value: a bar that sweeps until the work is done. *@
        <Progress Label="Preparing export" />

        <Progress Shape="ProgressShape.Circle" Value="72" Label="Profile" ShowValue />
        """;
}
